        "full_domain_true_overflow_exceptions": 56144,
        "full_domain_intermediate_shift_overflow_exceptions": 352,
        "silent_corruptions": 0,
        "note": "Cell::operator* uses 5-trit shift-and-add. Operands in [-10, +10] fit in three balanced trits (trits 0..2, 1+3+9=13 >= 10), whereas products in [-100, +100] can require five trits ([-121, +121]). Because operands fit in three trits, shifts stop at index 2, shifted operands (*this << i, i <= 2) have magnitude <= 90 <= 121, and partial sums remain representable in [-121, +121]; exhaustive testing confirms 441/441 pairs. Over the full [-121, +121]^2 domain (59,049 pairs), 352 pairs with |a*b| <= 121 throw std::overflow_error due to intermediate shift or partial-sum overflow."
      },
